{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Committed app-control interaction behavior: compact labels, failure wording, navigation, and summary parts. Changed 2026-09-18 with the conversation-coordination family: the read/list tools used to show their COMPLETED wording for a call that errored (this file described that as \"completed errors\"), which told the user a failed read had succeeded. Every tool in this family now uses the six label states — active/completed/following/failed/failedFollowing/other — and `error` maps to the failed pair. This is not a new idea bolted on: klaus_query already distinguished `error` -> `failed` in the same renderer, so the read/list tools were the inconsistent half of one family. `list_archived_threads` also became a first-class kind with real translations instead of falling through to the generic lowercase tool-name label. `interrupted` deliberately keeps the neutral completed wording: a cancelled turn may still have delivered its message, so claiming failure there would be as wrong as claiming success on an error. Added the coordination family (send/create/fork/wait/pin/unpin/archive/restore/rename) with its six label states. Send rows now open the full original prompt on click; navigation to a local target remains available inside the expanded row rather than stealing that click.",
  "behaviour": [
    "Completion no longer selects the read/list label independently from success: every tool in the conversation-coordination family uses the six label states (active/completed/following/failed/failedFollowing/other), so an errored call says it failed. `interrupted` keeps the neutral completed wording on purpose — a cancelled turn may still have delivered its message. `other` is a lookup fallback for an unmodelled state; no renderer path emits it, so it is not pinned as markup.",
    "A failed card that follows another action in a summary line uses the failedFollowing wording (nonLeading rows).",
    "Only a row with a nonempty threadId becomes a navigation button.",
    "Read rows keep localized lifecycle wording even when the target chat title is known; valid local targets remain clickable.",
    "Completed summary parts dedupe by host namespace and tool, in first occurrence order.",
    "Completed dynamic summary parts follow the generic activity categories and use Intl unit list formatting.",
    "Commentary is standalone; reasoning is omitted from activity units.",
    "A completed singleton becomes a direct row when its activity slice closes.",
    "Groups start collapsed; every read keeps its own navigation target when expanded.",
    "Active header key transitions defer until 1000 ms after the prior commit; completed summary is immediate.",
    "The activity shimmer starts after 600 ms, sweeps for 1000 ms every 4000 ms, and respects reduced motion.",
    "Disclosure opens and closes over 300 ms with cubic-bezier(.19,1,.22,1).",
    "Generic dynamic tools share the group, dedupe by exact tool identity, and format labels with lowerCase and upperFirst; they never navigate or disclose arguments/results."
  ],
